sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant U as User

    box rgb(238,248,242) GUI thread
        participant W as Window<br/>(wiring)
        participant V as ImageViewerWidget
        participant I as InteractionSet
        participant B as Behaviors
        participant R as Receivers<br/>(window, dialog, listener)
    end

    W->>I: addBehavior(...) for each behavior
    Note over I: kept sorted by priority,<br/>highest first
    W->>V: setInteraction(interactionSet)
    Note over V,I: the viewer owns the interaction set

    W->>V: setImage / displayFrame, setLayers, applyViewConfig
    Note over V: the viewer is passive.<br/>It only draws what it receives

    U->>V: mouse, wheel or drag and drop event
    V->>I: mousePress / mouseMove / wheel / drop(view, event)

    alt a behavior is capturing (mouse press, move and release only)
        I->>B: the capturing behavior only
        B-->>I: handled
    else no behavior is capturing (and for wheel and drag and drop)
        loop behaviors in priority order
            I->>B: handler(view, event)
            B-->>I: handled or not
        end
        Note over I,B: the first behavior that returns true<br/>stops the dispatch
    end

    B->>V: acts on the viewer<br/>(pan, auto-fit, pixel info, drag highlight)

    opt the behavior has something to report
        B-->>R: signal or listener call<br/>(image dropped, fullscreen requested,<br/>color picked, shape requested)
    end

    V->>I: cursorForEvent(view, ...)
    I-->>V: the active cursor of the capturing behavior,<br/>otherwise the available cursor of the<br/>highest-priority behavior
